<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅζομαι</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf.; 
			Act.
		 only in part.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅζοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					134
				</span></i>
			:—<i>stand in awe of, esp. gods and one's
			parents</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁζόμενοι . . Απόλλωνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτ᾽ οὖν μητέρ᾽ ἐμὴν ἅζευ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.401
				</span></i>
			; followed by inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χερσὶ δ᾽ ἀνίπτοισιν Διἴ λείβειν . .
					ἅζομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.267
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξείνους οὐχ ἅζεο . . ἐσθέμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.478
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅ. μή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.261
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς δή κεν .. ἅζοιτ᾽ ἀθανάτους;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					748
				</span></i>
			,cf.<i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				54
			</span></i>: used by <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> in lyr., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς οὖν τάδ᾽ οὐχ ἅζεται;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Eu.</u>
					389
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παλλάδος δ᾽ ὑπὸ πτεροῖς ὄντας
				ἅζεται πατήρ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς</span>) <i>respects . .</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1002
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅζονται γὰρ ὁμαίμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					652
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλόκαμον οὐδάμ᾽ ἅζεται</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				884
			</span></i> (all lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θανεῖν οὐχ ἅζομαι</span>
			<i>I fear</i> not to die . . , <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1116
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs. in
				part., <i>reverently, in holy fear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.200
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφί σοι ἁζ&lt;&gt;́μενος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				155
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>to be angry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				348
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅγιος.</span>)</div>
